      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I think a feature like this would be incredibly useful as not only does it cut down on 'spammy' uses of the chatbox in busy instances but can also help just clear up clutter from genuine chatbox communication\n\nan obvious example is someone using a chatbox to talk to friends at the front of an event, it seems like the entire room behind them currently sees this - i think it would also be useful if chatboxes not only respected earmuffs but just generally closer matched the range of voice falloff in the world, just so that people across the other end of a the room didn't have to see a chatbox from someone they can't even see let alone couldn't hear if they were using voice\n\ndue to the way text messages work as 'one and done' communication it might be nice if there was a bit of falloff where you could see a 'distant' chatbox and allow you some time to move closer to see it or something, in the same way you can hear someone in the distance with earmuffs and move towards them to hear them better",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
